TY  - CPAPER
TI  - Learning When to Defer to an Expert
AB  - A classifier that may defer a decision to a human expert should do so when the expert is more likely to be right. We give a consistent surrogate loss for learning the classifier and the deferral rule jointly, and show on three medical imaging tasks that the joint system is more accurate than either the classifier or the expert alone.
